cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "vidmag: Eulerian Video Magnification in hand-written CUDA, with five further backends"
message: >-
  If you use this software in work you publish, please cite both this
  implementation and the original method it implements.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kucuk
    given-names: Furkan
repository-code: "https://github.com/iamkucuk/eulerian-video-magnification-cuda"
url: "https://iamkucuk.github.io/eulerian-video-magnification-cuda/"
abstract: >-
  An implementation of Eulerian Video Magnification that amplifies colour and
  motion changes in video too small to see, together with the phase-based
  follow-up method. The primary implementation is hand-written CUDA C++ for
  NVIDIA hardware, using no tensor framework. Four further implementations —
  OpenCL, Apple's Metal, Vulkan, and PyTorch — reach Apple, AMD and Intel
  hardware and any future device with a standard driver, and a NumPy version
  checked against the original authors' published output serves as the
  correctness reference all of them are compared against by an automated test
  suite.
keywords:
  - eulerian video magnification
  - motion magnification
  - video processing
  - computer vision
